 ],
 "literal": "On the leafless beautiful branches, swarms of bees buzz / resembling breasts, soft buds blossomed of the Kongu tree / the first blossoms have arrived, but he has not returned, O friend! / In the night of sleep, sleep he forgot / even the bed of thick fragrant hair he does not think of / desiring to bring earned wealth, he who went / 'he has reached' indeed, saying so, comes the message.",
 "translation": "On the leafless, beautiful branches, swarms of bees buzz. The soft buds of the kōṅku tree, resembling beautiful breasts, have blossomed. The first flowers of spring have arrived, O friend, but he has not returned. He has forgotten sleep in the dark night of sleep; he does not even think of the bed of my thick, fragrant hair. He who went away desiring to earn wealth—the only message that arrives is, 'He has reached his destination.'",
 "modern": "இலைகள் இல்லாத அழகிய கிளைகளில் வண்டுக் கூட்டங்கள் ஒலிக்கின்றன. மார்பகங்களைப் போன்ற மென்மையான மொட்டுகள் மலர்ந்த கோங்கு மரத்தின் முதல் மலர்கள் வந்துவிட்டன; ஆனால் அவர் இன்னும் வரவில்லை, தோழி! தூங்குவதற்குரிய இரவில் அவர் தூங்குவதை மறந்துவிட்டார். நெய் பூசிய மணம் வீசும் கூந்தலாகிய படுக்கையையும் அவர் நினைத்துப் பார்க்கவில்லை. பொருள் ஈட்ட விரும்பிச் சென்றவர், தன் இருப்பிடத்தை அடைந்துவிட்டார் என்று மட்டுமே செய்தி வருகிறது.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her friend during the season of separation (pālai). The spring season has arrived, marked by the blossoming of the kōṅku tree, whose buds resemble breasts, and the buzzing of bees on the leafless branches. This season was the promised time of the hero's return, yet he has not come back. Instead of the hero himself, only a messenger or a rumor arrives saying that he has safely reached the distant land where he went to earn wealth. The heroine laments that he has forgotten sleep and does not even think of her fragrant hair, which used to be his bed, choosing instead to stay away for the sake of wealth.",
